---
title: "Correlated Radiographic Theory"
code: "RAD-215"
category: "radiography"
credits: "2"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/RAD-110"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: RAD 110, RAD 112 and RAD 121-221"
---

Presents intensive correlation of all major radiologic technology subject areas. Studies interrelationships of biology, physics, principles of exposure, radiologic procedures, patient care, and radiation protection. Lecture 2 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
